---
layout: base.njk
bodyClass: hub colors-hub
title: Stones by Color
permalink: /colors/
description: "Browse minerals, crystals and gemstones by color: red, orange, yellow, gold, green, teal, blue, purple, pink, brown, black, gray, white & clear, and multicolor."
---
<h1>🎨 Stones by Color</h1>
<p class="lead">Pick a color to see every stone that comes in it, listed alphabetically by name. Many minerals come in several colors, so they appear on more than one page.</p>
<div class="swatch-grid">
{% for c in site.colorPages %}
  <a class="swatch-btn" href="{{ c.url }}" style="--stone:{{ c.hex }};--sw:{{ c.grad }}">
    <span class="swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="sw-label"><strong>{{ c.label }}</strong><small>{{ c.count }} stones</small></span>
  </a>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% for c in site.colorPages %}{% if c.top.length %}
<section class="color-row">
  <h2><a href="{{ c.url }}"><span class="dot" style="--sw:{{ c.grad }}"></span>{{ c.label }}</a> <small class="muted">{{ c.count }}</small></h2>
  <div class="grid">{% for c2 in c.top %}{% set c = c2 %}{% include "card.njk" %}{% endfor %}</div>
</section>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
<p class="muted small">Colors come from Wikidata, the color line of Wikipedia mineral infoboxes, and Crystopedia's own palettes. About {{ site.stats.total - site.stats.colored }} rare minerals have no published color in those sources yet, so they aren't listed here.</p>
